Using conservation of mechanical energy.
Decrease in kinetic energy = Increase in gravitational potential energy
$\begin{array}{ll}
\Rightarrow & \frac{1}{2} m v^2=\Delta U \\
\Rightarrow & \frac{1}{2} m v^2=\frac{m g h}{1+\frac{h}{R}} \\
\Rightarrow & h=\frac{v^2}{2 g-\frac{v^2}{R}}
\end{array}
Substituting the values, we get
$\begin{aligned}
h & =\frac{\left(4.0 \times 10^3\right)^2}{2 \times 9.8-\frac{\left(4 \times 10^3\right)^2}{6.4 \times 10^6}} \\
& =9.35 \times 10^5 \mathrm{~m}=935 \mathrm{~km}
\end{aligned}
